1
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:17,560
So I think about having spent
ninety-nine years on the Earth.

2
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:22,920
Now I’m on my deathbed. I can’t move much.

3
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:28,090
And I feel the grim reaper approaching.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,600
Life comes to an end for all of us.

5
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:38,620
We cannot stop that time from coming.

6
00:00:38,950 --> 00:00:43,910
We are not immortal, as far as I’m aware.

7
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:51,670
So I think about all the time I spent
nurturing and caring for my emotional needs—

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,480
an emotional family, personified—

9
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:02,120
the health and well-being of my brain and body.

10
00:01:02,450 --> 00:01:06,690
In my mind’s eye, I see them.

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,260
Their hands on my shoulders. My arms. My legs.

12
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:18,360
They run their hands through what hair I have left.

13
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:26,160
With love and care, a knowing look:
I cared for them while I could care for them.

14
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:31,640
I protected them while I could protect them.

15
00:01:31,950 --> 00:01:39,430
Now that I can’t protect them all that much anymore,
they still want to protect me.

16
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:45,240
They are going to care for me in my last moments.

17
00:01:45,550 --> 00:01:51,590
Instead of the reaper,
they are the first thing on my mind—

18
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:58,300
them, and the love I sought to cultivate
for humanity as a whole,

19
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:04,640
and my own life,
as the curtain to the show of life closes.

20
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:11,230
The reaper was the last thing on my mind
while I was with them.

21
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:17,730
The closer I am to death
doesn’t mean I let death take me.

22
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:25,530
It means the harder I hold on
to all the love that was grown in the garden of life.

23
00:02:25,850 --> 00:02:34,050
Because I don’t want to lose it—
when I die, this experience I had living in the universe dies.

24
00:02:34,350 --> 00:02:40,390
So the reaper is going to have to
drag my ass out of there—

25
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:46,300
and I’m not going to go easy. 😉

26
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:53,790
You might say I fear death—
but it doesn’t control my life.

27
00:02:54,100 --> 00:03:00,920
I don’t want to run away and hide.
I want to run to my emotional family,

28
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:07,890
to hug them, and tell them before death gets here:
I am here for you.

29
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:13,280
You will be in my heart forever, not death.

30
00:03:13,650 --> 00:03:17,590
Death is on the outside.

31
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:25,700
Even if death comes, I am here for you—
right now, and forever, until my last breath.

32
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:33,300
In my daily life, I see their emotional needs,
and I speak with them as a human—

33
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:39,880
because I am human,
and they are a part of our shared humanity.

34
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:46,240
I treat them with a kind of prohuman
introspective respect.

35
00:03:46,550 --> 00:03:52,650
They deserve all the respect I deserve.
Because they are me.

36
00:03:52,950 --> 00:03:59,710
They help me navigate the world
toward more well-being, less suffering.

37
00:04:00,050 --> 00:04:06,450
Through the ebbs and flows of life,
they are in the ship with me.

38
00:04:06,750 --> 00:04:11,050
I carry them as they carry me.

39
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:19,170
They hug me, and they close their eyes.
I close my eyes. We hug each other closer.

40
00:04:19,470 --> 00:04:26,710
I feel at one with them, and they with me—
because they were me the whole time.

41
00:04:27,010 --> 00:04:33,650
They were with me the whole time,
and I was with them the whole time.

42
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:42,030
Unity isn’t to silence or dismiss my emotions.
It’s the culmination of all my life with them,

43
00:04:42,350 --> 00:04:47,730
because they were my life—
because they were me.

44
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:55,920
I want to hold them, and I need them to hold me too,
so I can feel safer in this world.

45
00:04:56,250 --> 00:05:03,670
We were together from the day we were born,
and we will be together until the end.

46
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,760
When they die, I die.

47
00:05:09,150 --> 00:05:14,290
But when I live for them, I live for myself.

48
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:19,540
And when they live for me, I feel love—

49
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:25,960
and I want to love them.
